  "knn": { tier: "A", status: "clean", batch: "Classical ML (MSL)", auditRounds: 2, lastAuditDate: "2026-07-11", verifiedBy: "2026-07-11 IST: independent blind audit of the ORIGINAL module found it structurally FAILED (zero metaphor register, 4 disconnected worked examples instead of 1 running example, dimensionality-curse claim asserted not shown, a genuine numeric contradiction between the stated O(d log n) formula and the asserted op count, 2 checkQuestions testing untaught material) -- full writer rewrite dispatched, built around ONE running example (music-streaming 'similar songs', tempo/amplitude toy geometry -> 256-dim production embedding, n=10M) with checkQuestions also rewritten to match. Round-1 post-rewrite audit found 2 must-fix: 'a thousand-fold improvement' for the ANN speedup was a real arithmetic error (actual ~430,000x, off by 2+ orders of magnitude) -- fixed with the division shown; the 0.48/0.94 curse-of-dimensionality ratios were asserted despite the text explicitly promising shown arithmetic -- fixed by adding the actual formula (1-spread/2)/(1+spread/2). Round-2 confirm audit independently re-verified both fixes by hand (2,560,000,000/5,952=430,107.5; formula reproduces 0.48 and 0.94 exactly from stated inputs) plus every other number in the module (183x tempo/amplitude ratio, z-scores, ANN op-count reconciliation, rerank cost, all 5 checkQuestions) -- came back clean PASS, no further rounds needed. node --check exit 0. 2026-07-11 14:29 IST NOTE: hash refreshed 64777cf0d94fca1a -> 62e4b403d06aaf40 after logistic_regression's QnA-pilot verification fixes landed elsewhere in this same shared file -- this module's own content confirmed untouched first via byte-level diff (lines 1-279 and everything from id:'regularization' onward identical between old and new file); documented whole-file-hash sibling-edit false positive, not new drift. | 2026-07-12 08:59 IST: verifiedFileHash refreshed 62e4b403d06aaf40 -> e51d0d9e65025307 after MSL Phase A remainder workflow (wf_c7935ddf-7e6) edited sibling module(s) in src/data/foundations/classicalMLModules.js -- this module confirmed untouched, fix methodology used count==1 targeted string replaces scoped to their own module only.", sourceFile: "src/data/foundations/classicalMLModules.js", verifiedFileHash: "e51d0d9e65025307" },
  "naive_bayes": { tier: "A", status: "clean", batch: "Phase 2 (5-module batch)", lastAuditDate: "2026-07-11", verifiedBy: "2026-07-11 14:51 IST: Cold blind audit (module was full-content but never independently audited) found and fixed 5 issues: interactivePrompt asked about word-count multiplicity the real BayesCalculator interactive can't demonstrate (rewritten to match its actual prior/sensitivity sliders); a numeric error claimed NB has '10,000 simple count estimates' when the correct figure for a binary classifier is 20,000 (one per word per class) — fixed; MCQ1's option D was actually true (not a valid distractor for a 2-answer question) — rewritten to be genuinely false; the module's own hero worked example set up per-word probabilities but never computed/resolved a verdict — added the computed spam-wins-4-orders-of-magnitude result; Bernoulli NB was under-explained relative to its Multinomial/Gaussian siblings — added a concrete short-text use case. Independently re-verified round-2 (verdict CLEAN) including hand-recomputing the hero-example numbers. node --check exit 0. | 2026-07-12 08:59 IST: verifiedFileHash refreshed 62e4b403d06aaf40 -> e51d0d9e65025307 after MSL Phase A remainder workflow (wf_c7935ddf-7e6) edited sibling module(s) in src/data/foundations/classicalMLModules.js -- this module confirmed untouched, fix methodology used count==1 targeted string replaces scoped to their own module only.", sourceFile: "src/data/foundations/classicalMLModules.js", verifiedFileHash: "e51d0d9e65025307" },
